Subject: [PATCH 03344/11362] [outer-loop] arc: PIECE 3 deliverable -- hybrid
 explorer 3/11 first-win, dominates both baselines

Hybrid = structured-first + random-restart-on-stall. Measured on 11 games: 3/11 first-win (lp85 via
structured @20 actions eff 2.0069; r11l @901 + sp80 @777 via random diversity) vs structured-only 1/11
and pure-random 3/11-but-lp85-inefficient. The hybrid DOMINATES both: same reachability as random but
keeps lp85's efficient win that pure-random sacrificed -> strictly higher averaged min(h/a,1)^2 score.
This is the first measured, shippable lever on the 0.08 wall: the submitted depth_first_ride explorer
over-commits to one branch and misses easy structure-missed wins (r11l/sp80); random-on-stall recovers
them without costing the efficient wins. The remaining 8 games are the genuinely-hard sparse-reward tail
(no denser signal; random gets 0 too) -- frontier research, not diversity-recoverable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
